 "post": {
  "title": "Ask This When You're Stuck #shorts",
  "description": "Stuck on a decision? Ask what you'd tell a friend. Psychologists Igor Grossmann and Ethan Kross (Psychological Science, 2014) found people reason more wisely about a friend's relationship problem than their own — 'Solomon's paradox', after the king famed for wise advice and poor personal choices. When people reflected on their own problem from a distanced, third-person perspective, the gap disappeared. #psychology #shorts #decisionmaking #selfhelp",
